node_modules
*.local.json
*.bak.*
.log/

# scratch drafts — dispatch bodies, probe output. they are written fast and
# reviewed loosely, so they are the likeliest place for an account id, an arn,
# or a hostname to slip into a PUBLIC repo (rule.forbid.dox-in-public-repo)
.temp/

# skill scratch — progress sentinels, rmsafe's trash, captured tool output.
# every path under it is a WORKING NOTE a skill wrote for itself, so it is
# per-machine by nature and belongs in no commit. same dox exposure as .temp/
.agent/.cache/

# PLAYS — a play lives in one of exactly two dirs, and only ONE is ignored.
#
#   .play/temporary/   IGNORED (below). a probe written to answer one question
#                      and then discarded, or a rollback that un-converges a
#                      test box. neither is a durable claim about this repo.
#   .play/permanent/   TRACKED. a discrimination probe under
#                      `rule.forbid.repair-plays` exception 2 — a clamp that
#                      must reach every box, so its absence cannot be silent.
#
# 🛑 there is no third dir. `.agent/playbooks/` is forbidden.
#
# ⚠️ the ignore below is not a convenience — it is an ENFORCEMENT. a scratch
# play that is never committed cannot rot into a clamp nobody runs, and a check
# earns its keep by RUNNING, not by a seat in a directory
# (gotcha.a-check-that-cries-wolf-gets-silenced, m.13).
#
# what a scratch play proved belongs in a BRIEF, as a measurement stated inline.
# what a run must prove belongs in `git.grove.provision test`.
#
# either dir is reachable by slug — the sender resolves it, and halts if a name
# is held by both:
#   rhx git.grove.send <grove> --play <name>
#   rhx play.run --play <name>            # tracked plays, on THIS box
.play/temporary/

# a RUNTIME lock — it names one machine's live process, so a commit of it
# either lies to the next machine or blocks it
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
